1
00:01:50,050 --> 00:01:53,220
Spin, Pinwheel, Spin

2
00:01:53,510 --> 00:01:54,430
– He won!
– He won!

3
00:01:55,470 --> 00:01:59,430
Arlong Park has fallen!

4
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,600
We did it, Nojiko!

5
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:02,600
Mr. Gen!

6
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:06,690
This... This isn't a dream, is it?

7
00:02:06,690 --> 00:02:08,610
I never thought this
day would come...

8
00:02:21,790 --> 00:02:25,420
Way to go, Luffy!
You backed me up perfectly!

9
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:31,090
Although, as the star of the show, I could've
used a little more time in the spotlight!

10
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:34,050
Man, talk about a nail-biter...

11
00:02:34,930 --> 00:02:39,510
Next time, wrap it up a bit
quicker, you damn jerk!

12
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:10,090
This is awesome!

13
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:25,140
Alright, that's enough of that!

14
00:03:26,270 --> 00:03:27,100
It's him...!

15
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,860
Today's my lucky day!

16
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:34,740
Well done. I watched the entire fight.

17
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:39,280
Fluke or not, I never once
imagined the fishmen would lose

18
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:42,080
to a band of no-name pirates like you.

19
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:46,620
However, thanks to you, I don't have
to give any money to Arlong,

20
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:50,960
and all the valuables in
Arlong Park are now mine!

21
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,300
Drop your weapons!

22
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:55,510
The credit for this incident
now belongs to me,

23
00:03:55,510 --> 00:03:57,430
Captain Nezumi of the Marines' 16th–

24
00:04:00,010 --> 00:04:00,640
Zoro!

25
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:04,850
We're celebrating our victory.
Don't ruin our fun.

26
00:04:10,230 --> 00:04:15,150
Y-You just try and lay a finger
on me! You'll regret it!

27
00:04:15,150 --> 00:04:16,570
Still running your mouth?

28
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:22,700
This is for shooting Nojiko...

29
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:27,620
and for tearing up Bell-mère's
tangerine grove.

30
00:04:27,620 --> 00:04:28,120
Huh?

31
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,210
Captain!

32
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:39,590
Thanks, Nami! That felt good.

33
00:04:39,590 --> 00:04:42,090
Give him another thousand of those!

34
00:04:48,270 --> 00:04:51,650
You Marines are gonna clean
up after these fishmen now!

35
00:04:51,650 --> 00:04:54,020
And you're gonna help
rebuild the town of Gosa!

36
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:58,110
And don't even think about touching
any valuables in Arlong Park!

37
00:04:58,110 --> 00:05:00,490
That money belongs to
the island! You hear me?!

38
00:05:00,490 --> 00:05:04,410
Ow! Ow! L-Loud and clear!

39
00:05:04,410 --> 00:05:05,990
And one last thing!

40
00:05:06,450 --> 00:05:08,200
Give me my money back!

41
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:13,670
I'll give it back! I'll give it back!
It's not worth it anymore...

42
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,510
You're gonna pay, you rotten pirates!

43
00:05:19,510 --> 00:05:22,090
You, with the straw hat!
Your name's Luffy, right?!

44
00:05:22,470 --> 00:05:25,100
I take it you're the captain?!
Mark my words!

45
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:28,060
Big things are in store for you!
You've made me mad!

46
00:05:28,430 --> 00:05:30,430
It's too late for regrets!

47
00:05:30,430 --> 00:05:34,190
I will have my revenge!
Just you wait and see!

48
00:05:34,190 --> 00:05:36,690
Big things are in store, he says.

49
00:05:36,690 --> 00:05:40,070
How does he know I'm gonna
be King of the Pirates?

50
00:05:40,070 --> 00:05:42,950
That's not what he means, dumbass!

51
00:05:42,950 --> 00:05:46,530
H-Hey, what do we do?! What if
something really does happen?!

52
00:05:46,530 --> 00:05:48,580
Huh?! Huh?! Tell me!

53
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:53,080
Alright, everyone!
We can't go having all the fun!

54
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:56,340
Let's tell the whole island
what happened here!

55
00:05:58,670 --> 00:06:00,130
Arlong Park...

56
00:06:00,130 --> 00:06:02,840
Arlong Park has fallen!

57
00:06:04,050 --> 00:06:08,060
You hurting anywhere, Zoro? Here?

58
00:06:05,430 --> 00:06:08,060
Huh? What're you– Hey!

59
00:06:17,190 --> 00:06:19,400
Good for you, Nami.

60
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:24,740
I can't believe we were
saved by pirates...

61
00:06:24,740 --> 00:06:26,740
Life's full of surprises.

62
00:06:43,550 --> 00:06:46,550
Really, Nami? You're still here?

63
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:49,560
Your friends have been
looking for you.

64
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:53,180
Hey, Nojiko...

65
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:53,680
Huh?

66
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:54,520
Mr. Gen...

67
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:55,140
Hm?

68
00:06:55,140 --> 00:06:57,650
If Bell-mère was still with us,

69
00:06:57,650 --> 00:07:00,610
do you think she'd stop
me from being a pirate?

70
00:07:01,230 --> 00:07:02,610
A pirate?!

71
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,990
Give me a break!

72
00:07:04,990 --> 00:07:08,240
There's no way she'd ever let her
precious daughter be a pirate!

73
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,910
She wouldn't stop you!

74
00:07:08,950 --> 00:07:09,910
Nojiko!

75
00:07:09,910 --> 00:07:11,080
Even if she tried...

76
00:07:11,870 --> 00:07:13,540
would you really listen to her?

77
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:17,540
Hell no!

78
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:21,500
I see...

79
00:07:24,170 --> 00:07:25,510
What's so funny, Mr. Gen?

80
00:07:28,470 --> 00:07:31,970
You two are definitely
Bell-mère's kids, alright.

81
00:07:31,970 --> 00:07:33,270
Mr. Gen?

82
00:07:33,270 --> 00:07:34,230
Nami.

83
00:07:34,230 --> 00:07:36,770
You've already made up
your mind, haven't you?

84
00:07:36,770 --> 00:07:38,310
Then live how you want to.

85
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:40,980
Just like your mother.

86
00:07:47,410 --> 00:07:48,610
He's still at it.

87
00:07:49,530 --> 00:07:52,410
Sounds like Zoro's going through it.

88
00:07:52,410 --> 00:07:53,910
You said it.

89
00:07:53,910 --> 00:07:56,870
It'd normally take two years to heal from those wounds!

90
00:07:58,620 --> 00:07:59,960
You moron!

91
00:08:00,460 --> 00:08:02,920
Trying to treat such
a grave injury on your own...

92
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,090
Oww!

93
00:08:04,090 --> 00:08:07,130
Honestly! Are you folks
really pirates?!

94
00:08:07,130 --> 00:08:08,380
Don't you even have...

95
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:10,470
a doctor on board?!

96
00:08:10,470 --> 00:08:12,890
A doctor? That'd be nice, too!

97
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:13,760
Luffy?

98
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:16,140
But a musician comes
first. Right, Zoro?

99
00:08:16,140 --> 00:08:17,390
Why's that?!

100
00:08:17,390 --> 00:08:19,650
'Cause pirates sing! Duh!

101
00:08:19,650 --> 00:08:22,310
Okay, but why does that come first?!

102
00:08:22,310 --> 00:08:24,320
Hello?! Hello?!

103
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:27,820
Marine Base (16th Branch)

104
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:26,190
Yes. This is Marine Headquarters.

105
00:08:26,190 --> 00:08:27,950
HQ?! Is this Marine HQ?!

106
00:08:27,950 --> 00:08:32,490
Hello! This is Captain
Nezumi of the 16th Branch!

107
00:08:32,490 --> 00:08:35,080
Marine code 00733!

108
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:39,250
Transponder Snail
16th Marine Branch

109
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:36,950
I have a request for HQ!

110
00:08:36,950 --> 00:08:39,330
No need to shout. I can hear you.

111
00:08:39,330 --> 00:08:47,470
Listen! There's a pirate wearing
a straw hat named Luffy!

112
00:08:43,290 --> 00:08:47,470
Transponder Snail
Marine HQ

113
00:08:47,470 --> 00:08:51,970
I deem him and his four crew
members enemies of the government!

114
00:08:52,010 --> 00:08:56,390
Marine HQ Information Office

115
00:08:52,430 --> 00:08:57,060
I deem him and his four crew
members enemies of the government!

116
00:08:57,060 --> 00:08:58,560
"Luffy..."

117
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:03,940
They took down Arlong Park's supposedly
invincible fishmen, the Arlong Pirates!

118
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:06,570
Given the threat that they pose,

119
00:09:06,570 --> 00:09:10,070
I've placed a sizable bounty
on the captain, Straw Hat Luffy!

120
00:09:10,070 --> 00:09:11,700
Sending a photograph now!

121
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:12,780
Roger that.

122
00:09:16,620 --> 00:09:17,500
Huh?!

123
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:20,250
You couldn't get
a better shot than that?!

124
00:09:20,250 --> 00:09:22,000
No, sir. I'm afraid not...

125
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:26,960
After a quick verification,
I will submit it for approval.

126
00:09:27,710 --> 00:09:31,630
Don't forget! He's a rotten pirate,
so it's dead or alive!

127
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:37,180
Put him on wanted posters
across the globe!

128
00:09:49,740 --> 00:09:51,700
Whew, I'm stuffed!

129
00:09:52,070 --> 00:09:55,070
It's nice to just eat for a change.

130
00:09:55,070 --> 00:09:56,950
Are your wounds healed up, Zoro?

131
00:09:56,950 --> 00:09:59,950
Some food and drink'll fix me right up.

132
00:09:59,950 --> 00:10:01,370
That so?

133
00:10:01,370 --> 00:10:04,750
But seriously, how long
is this stupid party gonna last?

134
00:10:04,750 --> 00:10:06,710
This is the third day now!

135
00:10:06,710 --> 00:10:08,050
What's wrong with that?

136
00:10:08,050 --> 00:10:11,670
If you're gonna celebrate,
might as well pull out all the stops.

137
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:15,510
Hey, Sanji! That melon you just had!

138
00:10:15,510 --> 00:10:16,890
Was there something on it?!

139
00:10:16,890 --> 00:10:19,270
What's with all that meat?!

140
00:10:19,270 --> 00:10:22,730
Sure was. It's prosciutto and melon,
so there was dry-cured ham on it.

141
00:10:22,730 --> 00:10:25,810
Ham and melon?! Sounds yummy!
Wh-Where's it at?!

142
00:10:25,810 --> 00:10:26,360
I dunno.

143
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:31,690
The village is one big buffet party right now.
Couldn't tell you where I got it.

144
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:33,700
He's long gone.

145
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:36,030
He's been eating non-stop
for three days!

146
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:39,030
As for me, that's enough food.

147
00:10:39,830 --> 00:10:40,910
It's about time I...

148
00:10:40,910 --> 00:10:42,580
go charm the ladies!

149
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:46,580
It is I, Captain Usopp!
The lovable and courageous hero

150
00:10:45,330 --> 00:10:46,580
Way to go, kiddo!

151
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:48,340
Can I have your autograph?!

152
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:50,130
who defeated the strongest
fishman leader of all!

153
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:54,930
Now how about an Usopp anthem?!

154
00:10:54,930 --> 00:11:00,680
♪ Who was it? Who was it? ♪
♪ Who beat the fishman? ♪

155
00:10:59,140 --> 00:11:00,680
What a bore.

156
00:11:01,060 --> 00:11:01,680
What is?

157
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:04,230
I thought you'd be more
down in the dumps.

158
00:11:04,230 --> 00:11:08,110
Like, "Why couldn't this have
happened before my daddy died?!"

159
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:09,480
Y'know?

160
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:13,070
That's how I felt at first.

161
00:11:13,070 --> 00:11:15,990
But now I'm thinking about the future.

162
00:11:15,990 --> 00:11:17,570
The future?

163
00:11:18,070 --> 00:11:21,370
That straw hat guy
and his friends helped us out.

164
00:11:21,740 --> 00:11:26,210
But tomorrow, we need
to make a fresh start by ourselves.

165
00:11:26,870 --> 00:11:31,420
There's no way we can forget the
past, and I don't think we need to.

166
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:35,510
What matters most
is what comes next!

167
00:11:35,510 --> 00:11:38,590
What now? What do we need to do?

168
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:42,470
From now on, we're the ones
who'll keep our villages going.

169
00:11:42,970 --> 00:11:44,770
That's how I see it, at least.

170
00:11:46,850 --> 00:11:47,600
Smartass!

171
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:48,850
Ow! Ow! Ow!

172
00:11:48,850 --> 00:11:51,860
Why are you pinching me?!
I don't understand! Why?!

173
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:54,110
And here I was hoping
to tease you again!

174
00:11:54,110 --> 00:11:58,110
You've teased me plenty,
you inked-up punk!

175
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:05,410
"Punk" is fine by me!

176
00:12:08,830 --> 00:12:09,830
Will it come off?

177
00:12:09,830 --> 00:12:13,500
I wish I could say it'd be no problem,

178
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:15,010
but I can't fully remove it.

179
00:12:15,630 --> 00:12:16,380
Yeah.

180
00:12:16,970 --> 00:12:20,970
I know it's stupid of me.
It'll be with me for life.

181
00:12:20,970 --> 00:12:23,760
I don't want anyone to see this!

182
00:12:24,430 --> 00:12:27,560
This... This tattoo...

183
00:12:27,560 --> 00:12:31,770
I don't even want
to be in Arlong's crew,

184
00:12:31,770 --> 00:12:34,230
but it's like I've been branded a pirate!

185
00:12:35,940 --> 00:12:37,240
Nami...

186
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:42,200
Nojiko! What's that?!

187
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,080
What, this?

188
00:12:43,870 --> 00:12:47,040
It's no big deal!
It's just a bit of art!

189
00:12:47,370 --> 00:12:48,960
Now we're matching!

190
00:12:56,010 --> 00:12:57,260
Say, Doctor...

191
00:12:57,970 --> 00:13:00,340
There is a tattoo that I want.

192
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:02,720
Here.

193
00:13:03,890 --> 00:13:05,260
Those two sure can dance!

194
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:09,180
Time for Usopp Anthem No. 185!

195
00:13:14,270 --> 00:13:15,900
Bell-mère...

196
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:20,150
Your little girls have grown
into tough, honorable women.

197
00:13:21,410 --> 00:13:24,330
It's like you're still here with us.

198
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:28,790
From here on out, we're gonna
live life to the fullest.

199
00:13:29,290 --> 00:13:32,790
We're only here because of
how much we've sacrificed.

200
00:13:32,790 --> 00:13:38,090
And that's exactly why we're
gonna smile and laugh like idiots!

201
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:41,590
Ham and melon!

202
00:13:41,930 --> 00:13:46,600
Wha...? There's no food around here.
Aw, crap. Guess I'll head back...

203
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:47,560
Hold it, boy!

204
00:13:48,850 --> 00:13:51,850
A grave? Did somebody die?

205
00:13:51,850 --> 00:13:54,060
Yeah. A long time ago.

206
00:13:54,690 --> 00:13:59,030
Oh, my deepest conveniences.

207
00:13:59,530 --> 00:14:04,160
Uh... Deepest compliments.
Wait. Deepest concussio–

208
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:06,410
Deepest condolences.

209
00:14:06,410 --> 00:14:08,120
Yeah, that.

210
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:09,410
Hey, boy.

211
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:13,960
Nami is going aboard your ship.
She's going to be a pirate.

212
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,960
It'll be a dangerous journey.

213
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:18,090
There's no way around that.

214
00:14:18,090 --> 00:14:20,760
I get it. But know this.

215
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:24,260
If you guys ever do anything
to take away her smile,

216
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:26,720
I'll kill you myself!

217
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:29,680
Sure. I'm not gonna do that, though.

218
00:14:30,350 --> 00:14:31,140
Got it?!

219
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:34,100
I got it!

220
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:02,130
I'm

221
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:02,130
leaving

222
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:02,130
this

223
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:02,130
behind.

224
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:02,130
It

225
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:02,130
belongs

226
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:02,130
to

227
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:02,130
the

228
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:02,130
village.

229
00:14:59,170 --> 00:15:02,130
Nami

230
00:15:07,050 --> 00:15:11,310
Wow! So much food today!

231
00:15:11,310 --> 00:15:14,560
Do you two know what today is?

232
00:15:14,890 --> 00:15:18,690
It's the anniversary
of the day I met you!

233
00:15:19,310 --> 00:15:21,690
The day you two
became my daughters!

234
00:15:21,690 --> 00:15:22,570
Wow!

235
00:15:26,530 --> 00:15:28,410
C'mon, stop crying!

236
00:15:28,410 --> 00:15:31,540
A storm destroyed
the grove. So what?

237
00:15:31,540 --> 00:15:36,000
I need you girls to be strong
and smile even when times are tough!

238
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:40,250
Do that, and I'm sure
you'll find happiness!

239
00:15:41,710 --> 00:15:43,920
You will. I promise!

240
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:46,760
Nami! Mind getting me the salt?

241
00:15:48,010 --> 00:15:50,720
First you learned to draw
sea charts, and now land maps!

242
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:54,270
I've been studying navigation, too!

243
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:56,390
Even navigation?!

244
00:15:56,390 --> 00:15:58,350
That's Nami's dream, after all!

245
00:15:59,060 --> 00:16:02,940
I'm gonna use my navigation skills
to sail all the world's seas!

246
00:16:02,940 --> 00:16:06,570
And then I'll make a map
of everything I see!

247
00:16:07,070 --> 00:16:11,530
That means this map of the island
is the first step toward your dream!

248
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:13,040
Yeah!

249
00:16:44,070 --> 00:16:46,740
It's over, Bell-mère.

250
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:50,820
It took eight years,
but we're finally free!

251
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:53,490
Me, and everyone else...

252
00:16:53,490 --> 00:16:55,950
It's just like you said.

253
00:16:55,950 --> 00:16:59,830
"If we survive, we'll be
happy someday."

254
00:16:59,830 --> 00:17:01,210
You were right!

255
00:17:01,210 --> 00:17:04,840
All the villagers are smiling from
the bottom of their hearts!

256
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:10,180
As for me, I'm thinking
of leaving the island!

257
00:17:11,130 --> 00:17:13,930
It'll be fine! Don't worry about it!

258
00:17:13,930 --> 00:17:17,640
They're all great people,
not to mention super tough!

259
00:17:19,270 --> 00:17:23,270
I've drawn so many charts
and maps over the last eight years,

260
00:17:23,270 --> 00:17:25,610
and this is the only one left.

261
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:32,200
But that's just it! This time,
I'm gonna draw charts for myself!

262
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:36,410
I'm gonna travel the world
with them—with my friends!

263
00:17:37,910 --> 00:17:40,330
That was my dream, so...

264
00:17:41,750 --> 00:17:42,830
So...

265
00:17:44,250 --> 00:17:47,590
So I'm not sure when I'll
come back to this island...

266
00:17:56,390 --> 00:17:58,430
Well... I'm off.

267
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:22,000
The Morning of Departure

268
00:18:24,790 --> 00:18:26,080
This the last of it?

269
00:18:26,080 --> 00:18:26,790
Yeah!

270
00:18:26,790 --> 00:18:27,380
Alright!

271
00:18:27,380 --> 00:18:28,630
All done loading?

272
00:18:28,630 --> 00:18:29,500
Yeah!

273
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:32,380
Right. We've got plenty
of provisions now.

274
00:18:32,380 --> 00:18:33,590
We're good to go.

275
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:36,760
We were only here a few days,

276
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:39,100
but we sure made a lot
of memories, huh?

277
00:18:39,430 --> 00:18:40,520
Yup!

278
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:51,070
We owe you so much for
everything you've done.

279
00:18:51,070 --> 00:18:54,490
We're gonna get back
to bounty hunting again!

280
00:18:54,490 --> 00:18:55,410
We part ways here,

281
00:18:56,110 --> 00:18:58,910
but we look forward to the day
we meet again somewhere!

282
00:18:59,910 --> 00:19:00,870
Take care!

283
00:19:01,500 --> 00:19:03,120
– You guys, too!
– You guys, too!

284
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:05,330
Well, it's about time
we shove off, too!

285
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:08,880
Hey, hold on a sec!
What about Nami?!

286
00:19:09,630 --> 00:19:11,050
Maybe she's not coming?

287
00:19:11,050 --> 00:19:13,090
Wh...?! Why not?!

288
00:19:13,590 --> 00:19:17,090
You! You made another
pass at Nami, didn't you?!

289
00:19:17,090 --> 00:19:18,350
Why would I do that?

290
00:19:18,350 --> 00:19:20,100
That reminds me...

291
00:19:18,350 --> 00:19:20,100
I know you did!

292
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:24,230
She did what she set out to do,
and she has no reason to be a pirate,

293
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:24,230
You can't stand that Nami
and I are all lovey-dovey!

294
00:19:24,230 --> 00:19:25,230
What're you, stupid?

295
00:19:24,230 --> 00:19:27,600
so maybe she'd be happier here...

296
00:19:25,230 --> 00:19:26,850
What did you say?!

297
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:29,060
Why can't I be happier?!

298
00:19:29,690 --> 00:19:32,730
If Nami isn't on the ship,

299
00:19:32,730 --> 00:19:36,070
then 98.72% of my reason
for being here is gone!

300
00:19:36,070 --> 00:19:39,070
Hey, you know, I couldn't find
that ham and melon anywhere!

301
00:19:39,570 --> 00:19:40,700
Hey! Where's Nami?

302
00:19:40,700 --> 00:19:43,620
That's the thing! Nobody's
seen her since this morning!

303
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:44,250
What?!

304
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:46,540
She's leaving all the money behind?!

305
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:48,750
The full 100 million berries?!

306
00:19:48,750 --> 00:19:51,040
She's going to travel
without her money?!

307
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:53,840
But she risked her life to earn it!

308
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:57,010
She says she'll just steal
some more, so it's all good.

309
00:19:58,390 --> 00:20:01,010
When she says something,
you can't change her mind.

310
00:20:01,390 --> 00:20:02,760
That fool!

311
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:06,480
We're the ones who still have
so much to thank her for!

312
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:12,900
– Nami!
– Nami!

313
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:14,280
Nami!

314
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:16,400
Hey, Nami!

315
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:16,400
It's Nami!

316
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:17,740
Get the ship moving!

317
00:20:24,290 --> 00:20:26,660
Huh? She started sprinting!

318
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:27,910
She said to get moving.

319
00:20:27,910 --> 00:20:28,500
Yeah, but...!

320
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:31,460
Is she really going to leave

321
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:35,300
without letting us thank
her or say goodbye?!

322
00:20:35,300 --> 00:20:35,880
No way!

323
00:20:36,210 --> 00:20:37,880
Set the sails!

324
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:44,260
H-Hey!

325
00:20:44,260 --> 00:20:45,930
They're setting off!

326
00:20:45,930 --> 00:20:48,690
Wait! We haven't thanked you yet!

327
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:51,650
Stop, Nami!

328
00:20:51,650 --> 00:20:53,110
At least let us thank you!

329
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:54,860
– Nami!
– Nami! Calm down!

330
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:58,860
Hold it! I won't let you leave like this!

331
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:02,120
Hey, you sure it's okay
to let her leave like this?

332
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:04,830
Why not? It's her decision.

333
00:21:23,050 --> 00:21:23,600
Nami!

334
00:21:32,190 --> 00:21:33,310
What gives?!

335
00:21:34,060 --> 00:21:35,070
Nami!

336
00:21:56,420 --> 00:21:56,960
She didn't!

337
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:59,710
– What's this...?!
– My wallet's gone!

338
00:22:00,090 --> 00:22:01,050
Mine, too!

339
00:22:01,050 --> 00:22:02,260
Same here!

340
00:22:07,310 --> 00:22:08,890
Take care, everyone!

341
00:22:08,890 --> 00:22:09,680
How...?!

342
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:13,980
– How dare you?! You rotten brat!
– How dare you?! You rotten brat!

343
00:22:14,940 --> 00:22:17,940
Hey, she hasn't changed a bit.

344
00:22:17,940 --> 00:22:19,780
She might just betray us again...

345
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:21,490
Nami! Good job!

346
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:25,780
You lousy cat burglar!

347
00:22:25,780 --> 00:22:26,700
Get back here!

348
00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:27,660
My wallet!

349
00:22:27,660 --> 00:22:29,080
You punk!

350
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:30,830
Come back anytime!

351
00:22:30,830 --> 00:22:31,960
Take care of yourself!

352
00:22:31,960 --> 00:22:33,710
We appreciate you guys!

353
00:22:35,210 --> 00:22:36,590
Boy!

354
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:40,420
Don't forget your promise!

355
00:22:44,470 --> 00:22:47,550
So long, everyone!
Until we meet again!

356
00:22:50,850 --> 00:22:52,560
She sure got us!

357
00:22:52,560 --> 00:22:55,350
My little sister's a piece of work!

358
00:22:56,810 --> 00:22:58,060
Have fun out there!

359
00:23:02,070 --> 00:23:04,320
Here, Genzo.

360
00:23:04,320 --> 00:23:06,620
A piece of paper?
What's this, Doctor?

361
00:23:07,200 --> 00:23:11,950
That silly girl. She never learns.
She wanted a new tattoo before leaving.

362
00:23:12,910 --> 00:23:14,290
What's this symbol?

363
00:23:14,750 --> 00:23:17,750
It's a tangerine
and a pinwheel, apparently.

364
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:22,420
Oh? Mr. Gen! What happened
to your pinwheel?

365
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:28,550
I won't be needing it anymore.

366
00:23:39,310 --> 00:23:41,570
Bell-mère, I'm off.

367
00:23:48,110 --> 00:23:51,410
Hold on, Mr. Gen!
Stay away from Nami!

368
00:23:51,870 --> 00:23:55,500
Aw, but I wanna see her smile, too!

369
00:23:55,500 --> 00:23:58,710
She starts crying because
you have such a scary face!

370
00:23:58,710 --> 00:24:01,210
Come on, what am I
supposed to do about that?!

371
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:02,380
I know!

372
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:06,300
If I just keep this right here,
it'll make you laugh, won't it?!

373
00:24:06,300 --> 00:24:08,340
Well, Nami?!

374
00:24:08,340 --> 00:24:11,970
Listen, I really don't think a silly ol'
pinwheel is gonna make Nami...

375
00:24:19,900 --> 00:24:22,020
Oh. She's laughing.

376
00:24:27,700 --> 00:24:31,370
The skies are clear
and the winds are fair.

377
00:24:31,370 --> 00:24:35,160
And the pinwheel
spins merrily for another day.
